<title>NETHERLANDS: KLM load factor rises to 69.8 pct in Jan.</title>
<headline>KLM load factor rises to 69.8 pct in Jan.</headline>
<text>
<p>AMSTERDAM, Feb 7 (Reuter )- Provisional traffic and load factor figures from KLM Royal Dutch Airlines (millions of tonne-kilometres unless otherwise stated):</p>
<p>			   Jan '97  Jan '96 Apr-Jan 96/97 Apr-Jan 95/6</p>
<p>TOTAL TRAFFIC</p>
<p>Traffic		    675.8    635.6     7,215.1    6,767.8</p>
<p>Capacity		   968.2    947.8     9,964.8    9,360.3</p>
<p>Load factor (pct)	 69.8     67.1	  72.4	 72.3</p>
<p>PASSENGER TRAFFIC</p>
<p>Passenger kilometres 4,102.2  3,684.0    41,996.5   38,235.9</p>
<p>Seat kilometres	5,529.8  5,172.8    55,612.6   51,331.0</p>
<p>Load factor (pct)	 74.2     71.2	  75.5	 74.5</p>
<p>FREIGHT TRAFFIC</p>
<p>Traffic		    290.3    288.4     3,257.8    3,164.6</p>
<p>Capacity		   472.7    490.7     4,963.9    4,770.9</p>
<p>Load factor (pct)	 61.4     58.8	  65.6	 66.3</p>
<p>NOTE: While KLM capacity expanded by two percent in January, traffic grew by six percent compared to January 1996.</p>
<p>January passenger traffic was up 11 percent while passenger capacity increased by seven percent.</p>
<p>Cargo traffic increased by one percent in January with a four percent decrease in cargo capacity.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
